[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{N}^\mathbb{N}, (f(x), \alpha) \in C\} = \{x \in X : \exists \alpha \in [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathbb{N}^\mathbb{N}, (x, \alpha) \in D\} = \pi_X(D).$$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mSince $D$ is closed and $\pi_X$ is a continuous projection, $\pi_X(D)$ is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124manalytic. Hence $f^{-1}(A)$ is analytic. $\square$[0m

