[38;2;124;124;124m^1_Y$. This means for every $A \in {\cal B}^1_Y$, $f^{-1}(A) \in {\cal B}^1_X$, [0m[38;2;124;124;124mi.e., $f$ is measurable from $(X, {\cal B}^1_X)$ to $(Y, {\cal B}^1_Y)$.[0m

